WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
A flower opens, fades and falls.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.110
Faces age.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.830
Even a river looks different every day.

4
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:13.530
Around 375 BCE, the Greek philosopher
Plato found that troubling.

5
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.520
He pictured prisoners,
chained since childhood,

6
00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.660
facing the wall of a cave.

7
00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.280
All they ever see are shadows.

8
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:26.180
So if everything you see is changing,
how could anyone know what's real at all?

9
00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:31.220
In this mission, you'll step inside Plato's
cave and decode what each part stands

10
00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:32.070
for.

11
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:37.170
Then you'll see how Plato split
reality, and each person, into two.

12
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.880
Your mission: find out how Plato thought
anyone could know what reality really

13
00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:42.450
is.
